{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Speak to all the congregation.</b> But does Aharon speak? Was it not already said, ״you shall speak״? Rather, they share honor with each other, and say to each other, Teach me — and the utterance goes out from between them both, as if both of them are speaking (Mekhilta)." "<b>Speak to all the congregation of Israel, saying, On the tenth of the month.</b> Speak today, on Rosh Chodesh, that they should take it on the tenth of the month." "<b>This one.</b> The Pesach of Egypt — its taking was on the tenth, and not the Pesach of generations (Pesaḥim 96)." "<b>A lamb per father's house.</b> For one family; now if they were many, could one lamb suffice for all of them? Scripture says, ״a lamb per house״ (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:30.883464226Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}